From: XG2010G OpenWrt Port <xg2010g@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: bypass rate adapter for USB fixed HSGMII

The AN7581 USB Multi-SerDes lane runs at the same fixed 2.5 Gbit/s rate
on both sides when used in 2500BASE-X mode.  Enabling the rate adapter in
this configuration prevents received traffic from reaching the XSI path.

Match the vendor SDK configuration by disabling the adapter and enabling
its RX/TX bypass paths.  Limit this to the USB PCS so that Ethernet, PCIe
and PON 2500BASE-X users keep their existing rate-adaptation behaviour.

Signed-off-by: XG2010G OpenWrt Port <xg2010g@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -547,11 +547,16 @@ static int airoha_pcs_config(struct phyl
 	/* Configure Interrupt for various modes */
 	airoha_pcs_interrupt_init(priv, index, interface);
 
-	rate_adapt = AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_RX_EN |
-		     AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_TX_EN;
+	if (data->port_type == AIROHA_PCS_USB &&
+	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX)
+		rate_adapt = AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_RX_BYPASS |
+			     AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_TX_BYPASS;
+	else
+		rate_adapt = AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_RX_EN |
+			     AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_TX_EN;
 
	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII)
		rate_adapt |= AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_RX_BYPASS |
			      AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_TX_BYPASS;

	/* AN Auto Settings (Rate Adaptation) */
